From da4b783e34bd05d7451a6f904fbf567af1215f99 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yzddmr6 <46088090+yzddmr6@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 15:04:15 GMT
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] drm/msm/shrinker: Only block for active BOs from kswapd

can_block() lets direct reclaim wait for active BOs to become idle, up
to 10 jiffies per BO.  Direct reclaim runs in the task that allocates,
and for a GPU driver that is often a task the GPU and the desktop
depend on: the compositor, or a task in the submit ioctl that holds the
reservation locks of the BOs it submits and allocates while pinning
them or for its submit tables.  Waiting there for the GPU turns memory
pressure into a stall of that task for as long as the scan takes, and
of everything that waits for the locks it holds.  When most BOs are
busy, as with userspace drivers that list every BO in each submit, the
scan runs into the timeout on BO after BO.

Other DRM drivers do not block on the GPU in direct reclaim.  i915
reaps active objects only from kswapd, see commit 5763ff04dc4e
("drm/i915: Avoid GPU stalls from kswapd") and commit 1d24ad457c54
("drm/i915: Allow kswapd to pause the device whilst reaping").  TTM
based drivers such as xe use ttm_bo_shrink_avoid_wait(), added by
commit 70d645deac98 ("drm/ttm: Add helpers for shrinking"), which only
lets kswapd wait for the GPU.

Do the same, and only let kswapd run the blocking active_purge and
active_evict stages.  This changes the policy of commit df0f439e3926
("drm/msm/shrinker: Fix can_block() logic"), which also allowed any
direct reclaim to block.  Direct reclaim still purges and evicts idle
BOs without waiting.  The eviction_can_block parameter keeps its
meaning and still disables blocking entirely.

Fixes: 025d27239a2f ("drm/msm/gem: Evict active GEM objects when necessary")
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem_shrinker.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem_shrinker.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem_shrinker.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem_shrinker.c
@@ -28,12 +28,17 @@ static bool can_swap(void)
 	return enable_eviction && get_nr_swap_pages() > 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * Only kswapd waits for active BOs to become idle.  Direct reclaim runs in the
+ * allocating task, which may be the compositor or a task submitting GPU work
+ * and holding the locks of the BOs it submits, so waiting there for the GPU
+ * stalls that task, and everything waiting on it, for the length of the scan.
+ */
 static bool can_block(struct shrink_control *sc)
 {
 	if (!eviction_can_block)
 		return false;
-	return (sc->gfp_mask & __GFP_DIRECT_RECLAIM) ||
-	       (current_is_kswapd() && (sc->gfp_mask & __GFP_KSWAPD_RECLAIM));
+	return current_is_kswapd() && (sc->gfp_mask & __GFP_KSWAPD_RECLAIM);
 }
 
 static unsigned long
